cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use RoboDE in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "RoboDE"
abstract: >-
  RoboDE is a robotics IDE for setting up robots, building scenes and running
  task plans. A task described in plain English is split into tasks for one or
  more robots, converted into calls from each robot's own function catalog, and
  checked for units, joint limits, reach, inverse kinematics and collisions
  before it runs in simulation: a built-in simulator, or NVIDIA Isaac Sim.
  It runs in a browser or an Electron desktop window.
authors:
  - given-names: Paramesh
    family-names: Sriram
version: 0.4.1-alpha
date-released: 2026-11-07
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Theboss12k/RoboDE"
url: "https://theboss12k.github.io/RoboDE/"
keywords:
  - robotics
  - robotics IDE
  - task planning
  - multi-robot systems
  - large language models
  - simulation
  - NVIDIA Isaac Sim
  - ROS 2
  - URDF
  - motion planning
